 "note": "Rims located by hand in data/labeling/rim_bigrings/label.html, two clicks per ring (its left edge, then its right). The queue comes from mine_big_rims.py, which finds large orange flattened blobs by colour and shape -- it fires on the scoreboard, red hoardings and the centre-court logo too, so every entry here was confirmed by eye against its frame.\n\nALL 38 were then re-rendered with the ellipse drawn on the frame and checked. One was wrong -- 5430 s came back 788 px wide, spanning most of the picture rather than a ring, because both clicks landed badly on a ring truncated by the left frame edge -- and it is dropped here. That check is not optional: a label read back from the tool that produced it proves nothing.",
